    Player: "Ferbli is a traditional Hungarian vying (betting) game that was extremely popular in the 19th and early 20th centuries. It is closely related to Poker and is played with a 32ndcard Germanndsuited deck. The game involves multiple rounds of betting where players can 'vye' (bet) or 'pass'. Hand rankings are based on combinations of rank and suit, with 'Four of a Kind' and the 'Banda' (four cards of the same suit) being the most soughtndafter hands. In rural Hungary and Transylvania, it remains a cultural staple of cafÃ© life.",
